PUT {{baseUrl}}/readinglists/{{readingListId1}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "read": true
}


### 6.7 Get User 1 profile with all reading list entries -> Expected: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{user1Id}}


### 6.8 Filter User 1 reading list by ?read=true -> Expected: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{user1Id}}?read=true


### 6.9 Filter User 1 reading list by ?read=false -> Expected: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{user1Id}}?read=false


### 6.10 Invalid ?read= query param -> Expected: 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{user1Id}}?read=maybe


### 6.11 Get non-existent user by id -> Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/999999


### ============================================================================
### 7. LOGOUT & DISABLED USER ENFORCEMENT (EXERCISE-25)
### ============================================================================

### 7.1 Logout User 2 -> Expected: 204 No Content
### Deletes User 2's session row from `sessions`.
### Check in to psql: psql postgres://postgres:root@localhost:5432/blog_db
### and run in psql: `SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE user_id = <user2Id>;` (should be empty).
### <user2Id> ~= 12 or 13, currently
### also run SELECT * FROM sessions;
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}


### 7.2 Reuse User 2's logged-out token -> Expected: 401 Unauthorized ("session invalid")
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}

{
  "title": "Post-Logout Attempt",
  "author": "Dean Bug",
  "url": "https://example.com/post-logout",
  "likes": 1,
  "year": 2024
}


### 7.3 Disable User 1 in psql before running 7.4 and 7.5:
### Run in psql:
###   UPDATE users SET disabled = true WHERE username = 'barrybee@yahoo.com';


### 7.4 Protected request with disabled user's active token -> Expected: 403 Forbidden ("account disabled")
### Even though User 1 still has a valid JWT and session row, `tokenExtractor` rejects disabled accounts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "title": "Disabled User Blog Attempt",
  "author": "Barry Bee",
  "url": "https://example.com/disabled-attempt",
  "likes": 1,
  "year": 2024
}


### 7.5 Login attempt while User 1 is disabled -> Expected: 401 Unauthorized ("account disabled")
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 7.6 Re-enable User 1 in psql before running 7.7:
### Run in psql:
###   UPDATE users SET disabled = false WHERE username = 'barrybee@yahoo.com';


### 7.7 Login after re-enabling User 1 -> Expected: 200 OK with new token
### Note the old token has not been superseded or revoked by the new token.
### Assume logged in on two separate devices.
# @name loginUser1AfterReenable
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{user1Email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}